=== briefing M5_1
About the Redhead Brigand's property
#show Hero 3
#show Smith 5
#show Map00 4
#ANIMATION 29
#CAMERA 5
#phrase Hero  1
Listen, I  found this map in the Redhead Brigand's bag - the one who conversed with the Orc. As far as I understand it, it has to do with some object the Orcs have. Look, there is also a picture of a Seer with a key...
#hide Map00
#show Map00 5
#ANIMATION 29
#CAMERA 7
#phrase Smith  2
Well, let us have a wee look, shall we?... Aha! There is a picture of a sarcophagus with a Magic Bit in it!
#ANIMATION 32
#CAMERA 10
#phrase Hero  3
Do you mean a rune?
#ANIMATION 9
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Smith  4
No, runes are different. And Bits are... uhhh... Toad's breath! I don't know what they are, but when the Witch lived in the village she used to pay good money for them. And I think she will not be too mean even now, if someone offers goodies like that to her... and we split the profits!
#ANIMATION 29
#CAMERA 6
#phrase Hero  5
I have not found anything yet and you talk about the splitting of profits! Look, there is a Troll here and something which looks like the entrance to a cave. Do you know where this is?
#ANIMATION 7
#CAMERA 7
#phrase Smith  6
Aye, the Troll cave is to the northeast of the foothills. You can get into the cave quite easily: the Troll who guards it is big but he is so stupid, anyone could fool him. But getting further into the cave - that's another story.
#ANIMATION 9
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Smith  7
Orcs are wily big devils, they are not only good fighters but they also make very clever things. Right next to the entrance to that cave there is a wee crevice with a drawbridge. I found out how it works, but I could not lower that bridge: to do that, one needs a certain small part.
#ANIMATION 29
#CAMERA 10
#phrase Hero  8
Well, why not make one, then?
#hide Map00
#show Map00 4
#ANIMATION 45
#CAMERA 9
#phrase Smith  9
And who will give me the blueprint - you? Also, don't forget - each Orc tribe has their own secrets and if I had, say, a mechanism for the bridge of the Island Orcs, it would not work with the Cave Orcs' bridge.
#hide Map00
#show Map00 5
#ANIMATION 14
#CAMERA 6
#phrase Hero  10
Does that mean that Orcs of different tribes do not trust each other?
#ANIMATION 29
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Smith  11
That is the point! I heard a rumor that the Island Orcs sent a Goblin party to steal a bridge mechanism from the Cave Orcs, and the Captain's people took it away from them.
#ANIMATION 31
#CAMERA 7
#phrase Smith  12
 So why not try to squeeze that thing from Gort? Show him some respect, do something for him... He will be indebted to you, and all you have to do is ask for it.
#hide Smith
#ANIMATION 30
#NOLIPS
#CAMERA 10
#phrase Hero  13
The Tightfist is the Tightfist. For him, the world only consists of money and debts. Maybe the Elder is right to be suspicious about him...
#DESC To himself

=== briefing M5_3
About the Orcs from the foothills
#show Hero 1
#show Smith 2
#ANIMATION 6
#CAMERA 5
#phrase Hero  1
The Orcs are not so frightening as Gort pictures them! I am surprised you never managed to scare them off yourselves.
#ANIMATION 7
#CAMERA 7
#phrase Smith  2
It is not so easy, you know. The thing is, the tribe which settled in the Foothills is not all that strong, but they have a very clever Seer living with them.
#ANIMATION 9
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Smith  4
He learned to control the magic pyramid - there is one right near the settlement. A funny thing really - it is an ancient device but works as good as new, damn it! So anyone who comes close to it gets a very nice lightning blast.
#ANIMATION 14
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Smith  5
But if someone could kill that Seer and switch the pyramid off, the Orc tribe would start to behave themselves very quickly. But I fear that no one could fight their way through to the Seer and I know that none of our men is capable of getting there by stealth to do the job quietly with a knife.
#ANIMATION 9
#CAMERA 10
#phrase Hero  6
Let us suppose I could do that.
#ANIMATION 31
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Smith  7
God bless you, Chosen! If you do that I will be eternally grateful, because I do want to be able to walk around the Foothills freely. And of course I would show my gratitude in a quite tangible way - if only you could deal with the Orcs!

=== briefing M5_4
About the seer and the pyramid
#show Hero 1
#show Smith 2
#ANIMATION 29
#CAMERA 9
#phrase Smith  1
God bless you, Chosen! Now we can walk in the Foothills safely. I promised to reward you, and I shall keep my word!
#ANIMATION 45
#CAMERA 2 -30 8 3
#phrase Hero  7
Oh by the way, where is your source of money here in Gipath? I was told there was no king here, but now I see genuine royal coins. How is this?
#ANIMATION 9
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Smith  8
Well, that is no mystery. Gipath was not always the desolate place it is nowadays - in ancient times other people lived here, nothing like us, you understand! But they disappeared without a trace, leaving only ruins behind... And the coins - well, apparently that is their legacy.
#ANIMATION 7
#CAMERA 10
#phrase Hero  9
So anyone who takes a good look around the ruins can become the first man in the village who is richer than you or Erfar?
#ANIMATION 15
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Smith  10
That is a possibility, aye.  But the problem is, the easily accessible places have been cleaned out a long time ago. And elsewhere, there are more unpleasant things than money awaiting the unwary searcher...
#ANIMATION 11
#CAMERA 9
