=== briefing R54
Talk with the Great Magician
#show Hero 3
#show Rick 4
#show Deva 5
#CAMERA 1
#ANIMATION 5
#phrase Rick  1
In our people's legends, fortune has always been presented as a wild horse which gallops wildly and has no mane to hold on to. Not everyone can  mount it, and fewer still can stay on it for very long. In Ingos you held fortune in your hands very tightly - so do not let it slip in Suslanger! There are a lot of people there who would love to see you thrown off into the dirt...
#ANIMATION 15
#CAMERA 10
#phrase Hero  2
There were enough of those in Ingos too. Diera alone was a prime example!
#ANIMATION 14
#CAMERA 1
#phrase Deva  3
Do not remind me of her! That woman!  I do not know words bad enough to describe that creature. Diera imagined me to be her rival for the affections of the Governor!
#ANIMATION 7
#CAMERA 12
#phrase Deva  4
How I tried to convince her I do not care about anyone but At-Zako - she never listened, not once. I still shiver when I think about those catacombs where she held me prisoner! What a good thing At-Zako will never experience that dreadful damp and cold!
#CAMERA 1
#ANIMATION 6
#phrase Rick  5
My knowledge of other lands is poor but what I do know of Suslanger is that it is neither cold nor damp. But I cannot guarantee that the climate will make our sojourn there very pleasant. 

=== briefing R54_1
About the Khadaganian empire
#show Hero 1
#show Rick 2
#CAMERA 9
#ANIMATION 6
#phrase Rick  1
If I were to choose a new place to live, the Khadaganian Empire would be the last choice. The state is founded on brute force and every Khadaganian is a master of those below him and a slave of those above him.
#CAMERA 11
#ANIMATION 6
#phrase Rick  2
But even the highest-ranking Khadaganian citizens are slaves to Emperor Neseb, a powerful Magician who has managed to concentrate more power in his hands than any other monarch before him. And though Suslanger is considered to be the Empire's backyard, you are going to find it very, very difficult - even there.

=== briefing R54_2
Go to Khadagan
#show Hero 1
#show Rick 2
#CAMERA 11
#ANIMATION 6
#phrase Rick  1
There is a Portal here in Gipath leading to Suslanger - it is a remnant of the bygone days of the Joons. It would be foolish not to use it - so you will travel to Suslanger by means of the Portal. Be careful and remember that anyone you meet may turn out to be an informant!

=== briefing R72
About the Khadaganian quest
#show Hero 3
#show Rick 4
#show Deva 5
#CAMERA 1
#ANIMATION 6
#phrase Rick  1
So you came back alone. The Dragonet saw what happened to you in Khadagan, but he is too young to understand the meaning of events. So - I await a full explanation!
#DESC (Severely)
#ANIMATION 32
#CAMERA 12
#phrase Deva  2
Oh great Tka-Rik! You expected to see your fellow Joon, while I waited for my lover... so tell me who is closer to despair now? But l still beg you not to be angry with this man. He may have failed in his quest, but he barely avoided death! Is that not worthy of respect - at the very least?
#CAMERA 11
#ANIMATION 3
#phrase Rick  3
Fair enough, Lu-a... I am afraid that I allowed my disappointment to turn into anger. I regret that, Zak, and I ask you to forgive me. But please, tell me what happened?
#ANIMATION 31
#CAMERA 6
#phrase Hero  6
I am afraid I will have to disappoint you! At-Zako is not in Khadagan, he used a teleportation amulet. I do not think a Great Magician would find it hard to find out where the amulet took him? But we also have yet another problem.
#ANIMATION 3
#CAMERA 10
#phrase Hero  7
The man has been subjected to a transformation spell, so no one knows what he looks like now! Frankly, I have no idea how I can find him!
#CAMERA 11
