=== briefing t43
About the body which has been found
#show Hero 1
#show Trapper 2
#ANIMATION 45
#CAMERA 2
#phrase Hero  1
I found the body of a man, and it looks like it was Snoop. Look how he was killed...
#show Hero 3
#show DriadArrow00 5
#show Trapper 5
#ANIMATION 61
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Trapper  2
Oh dear! Woodsfolk shoot such arrows out of their tubes! And you can always tell whose arrow it was - each tribe has its own colors and signs!
#hide DriadArrow00
#show DriadArrow00 3
#ANIMATION 11
#CAMERA 2
#phrase Hero  3
What Woodsfolk? We never heard of them where I come from!
#hide DriadArrow00
#show DriadArrow00 5
#ANIMATION 62
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Trapper  4
You live and learn, boy! I thought they were known throughout Ingos, but apparently that is not so. Briefly, they are tiny humans who live in the woods. I often see them and I even know some of them. I will tell you more about them later if you wish, just ask me.
#hide DriadArrow00
#show DriadArrow00 3
#ANIMATION 11
#CAMERA 2
#phrase Hero  5
I will not. Meanwhile could you tell me about this arrow and which tribe it belongs to?
#hide DriadArrow00
#show DriadArrow00 5
#ANIMATION 61
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Trapper  6
I cannot read the signs on arrows, that is the problem! Only the Woodsfolk can help you there. But I will tell you who can help.
#hide DriadArrow00
#show Hero 1
#show Trapper 2
#ANIMATION 63
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Trapper  7
Captain Tilvar has been looking for an excuse to subdue the Woodsfolk for a long time now and now you find a man killed by one of their arrows. The Guards would definitely go for a punitive expedition! So it would be in the Woodsfolks' best interests to find out which tribe is responsible.
#ANIMATION 44
#CAMERA 2
#phrase Hero  8
You mean I should go to them and somehow make them talk to me? Is that possible?
#ANIMATION 62
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Trapper  9
Yes it is, but you will have to risk your hide to do it, sonny. You see, there are several Woodsfolk clans with permanent feuds going on between them. For example the White Clan recently kidnapped the Keeper of the Green Clan and now they hold him captive.
#ANIMATION 61
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Trapper  10
You see, each Clan has its own Sacred Flower, to them like banners are to our army. And Keepers look after these flowers. So if you free the Keeper of the Green Clan, he will give you the Sacred Flower to bring to the Clan. After that their Chief will just have to talk to you!
#ANIMATION 3
#CAMERA 2
#phrase Hero  11
Excellent! Tell me where I can find the Keeper!
#ANIMATION 63
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Trapper  12
Listen carefully, sonny. After you leave the city go west across the lake. When you find the prison where the Keeper is held, do not forget to switch off the trap - first! The White Clan Seer has an evergreen leaf - take it and place on the altar in front of the prison. I mean, the Woodsfolk call it an altar but it looks more like a rotten stump covered with mushrooms to me.
#ANIMATION 44
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Trapper  14
And after you get the Sacred Flower go to the Green Clan! The road there is not difficult: go south from the city and you will find it. Their Chief is called Grey Leaf, I know him.

=== briefing t43_1
About Karansul
#show Hero 1
#show Trapper 2
#ANIMATION 61
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Trapper  1
Karansul has me by the throat with both hands. All the locals hate him. Everyone is in debt to him, he buys our trophies for a trifle then sells them for three times more. But woe betide he who tries to find another buyer! Karansul is in league with the local rough element. One wrong move and he sends his cutthroat friends to deal with you. And that, my friend, is a goodbye of a permanent nature.
#ANIMATION 15
#CAMERA 2
#phrase Hero  2
Yes, I can see it is serious. But can you not think of a way to put some pressure on this vermin?
#ANIMATION 11
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Trapper  3
Let us make an honest agreement - you help me and I will help you. And if you do something for me, I will tell you all I know about the merchant. All right?
#ANIMATION 11
#CAMERA 2
#phrase Hero  4
What do you want me to do?
#ANIMATION 62
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Trapper  5
Quite simple... soon a fur buyer from the capital will come to this area. He offers good prices for skins, nothing like our mean pirate here. But I cannot get to the meeting place where he collects the skins, because Karansul's... ruffians will have their eyes on me.
#show Hero
#show Trapper
#show SquirrelSkin 5
#ANIMATION 44
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Trapper  6
But if you could take my skins there... then we could have a nice chat about the merchant! The road to the meeting place is not difficult, but the problem is, it is located in Karansul's domain. So you can understand my wariness.
#hide  SquirrelSkin
#show SquirrelSkin 3
#ANIMATION 46
#CAMERA 2
#phrase Hero  7
All right, agreed. I will get your skins there, but first of all, tell me how I find the place...
#hide  SquirrelSkin
#ANIMATION 62
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Trapper  8
That is easy... when you reach Karansul's domain, go to the first valley to the south. There is an old tent there with a fire burning. Near that fire are a number of forks. Hang the skins on those forks and you are done!
#ANIMATION 44
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Trapper  9
Just do not go wandering around there: there is a Guard unit in that area. Times are troubled, so the Guards will be inclined to shoot first and ask questions later.

=== briefing t43_2
More about the Woodsfolk
#show Hero 1
#show Trapper 2
#ANIMATION 11
#CAMERA 2
#phrase Hero  1
You wanted to tell me about the Woodsfolk and asked me to remind you. Well, tell me!
#ANIMATION 61
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Trapper  2
Oh yes, that's right! Woodsfolk are more or less "Children of Nature", you know. They do not build houses, do not work the fields and of course they have no towns at all. But they are far from stupid, it is just that their minds work differently from ours.
#ANIMATION 62
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Trapper  3
And of course because of that humans do not understand them and... either do not like them or... are afraid of them. Look at our Captain of the Guards: he is so brave... he always promises to deal with those Woodsfolk once and for all. Why do you think he does that? Because he is afraid, that is why...
#ANIMATION 63
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Trapper  4
But one should not be afraid of them! On the contrary, we could learn from them: for example, can any human tame a unicorn? No! And Woodsfolk do it all the time, as if it were second nature to them. And they know the woods better than I do, even though I have been a hunter since I was a kid!
#ANIMATION 61
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Trapper  5
Actually, they are not really interested in humans. But if someone angers them, his prospects will indeed be grim. Woodsfolk may be small but they are hard to fight. They have a special weapon: a tube out of which they blow little poisoned arrows, just like the one which skewered the snoop.
#ANIMATION 45
#CAMERA 2
#phrase Hero  6
What harm can that little funny thing do? It will not even penetrate even a leather breastplate, will it?
#ANIMATION 46
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Trapper  7
Even if it was a mithrill one! There is a chink in every armor and the Woodsfolk will hit it all right, never fear. 
#ANIMATION 61
#CAMERA 3
#phrase Trapper  8
Then there are the tame unicorns. Those beasts are beautiful but if they get angry you will wish you had never seen that particular kind of beauty before! And there is one thing more... Woodsfolk know magic.
#ANIMATION 9
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Trapper  9
So that is the kind of little fellows we have around here. If you get on the wrong side of them, expect trouble, but if you manage to make friends with them, value it. A friendship like that could be very useful!

=== briefing t45a
About the Sacred Flower
#show Hero 1
#show Trapper 2
#ANIMATION 9
#CAMERA 11
#phrase Trapper  1
You got the Sacred Flower - now the Woodsfolk will talk to you. I think I told you before: to find the Green Clan, go due south from the city!

